  "result": "The O3 lesson is written, with a short quiz ready. Both review passes ended on \"revise\", so it still has known problems.\n\n- **Lesson:** `lessons/0001-context-and-memory.html`, 60 minutes. It runs one makerspace request through the context window, keeping the window small, retrieval from long manuals, notes that last between sessions, and pricing a design on paper.\n- **Quiz:** `quizzes/0002.json` has five items on O3, with its key in `keys/0002.json`. Ask me when you want to take it.\n\n**Problems still in the lesson:**\n- **Too dense for you.** It's heavier than your preferences ask for. Most parts define terms before showing the example, and there are seven headed sections instead of six.\n- **Review items I didn't fix.** Some misconception boxes lack a concrete case. Part 3 has two worked examples. A few practice items give no feedback on your own attempt.\n- **What I did fix.** I corrected the price and token-rule wording and the cost-ratio claim, and I added a citation.\n- **Community link.** The only link is Anthropic's community page, and I didn't open the Discord or subreddit it lists.\n\nI didn't write a cheat sheet this time. `NOTES.md` is updated, and the review details are in `review-records/0001-lesson.md`.\n\nShould I rewrite the lesson shorter and example-first? I think that fits how you learn better.",
